ar  is in orange and they also help you a  little bit for example for the future  subjunctive  cuando e es que ser or cuando tu es que  seres  so that they they help you with it so  in all i just think it's an it's an  excellent tool here again i find i can't  remember from studying these lists but  it does help me to notice so i start to  notice a little more when i'm listening  you know how the ar verbs er verbs ir  verbs uh perform in different tenses so  all of these things help me to notice  however  you know these are like as obviously  that's like the 20 activity the 80  activity is just the massive reading and  listening and armed with this um you  know having become a little more alert  because of looking at the nuts and bolts  then i become a little more attentive  when i'm listening and reading  my main activity has been massive  listening and reading  and today i worked all day in the garden  actually i'm quite exhausted  and so i had on i had my  i had my uh nano here  and i had these wonderful  uh wireless  uh head headphones so i didn't cut  anything and didn't get entangled in the  bushes or anything while i was listening  although i was sweating profusely  and i was listening to  uh  the kite runner in portuguese again some  years ago when i got interested in  portuguese i sent away for some audio  books from brazil and this is one of the  ones that i got it's it's okay  i the other day i was listening in my  car to uh arte de guerra which uh  so i mean my wife now has gone to  toronto to visit with her family so  i'm doing a lot of work around the house  cleaning things up and that sort of  thing i played a couple of games of golf  with friends so  unfortunately my friends don't  appreciate it if i listen while we're  playing golf but it's a 40-minute drive  there 40-minute drive back i'm listening  uh  so  there was oh another one of my favorites  many years ago when i was four or five  years ago it was uh ruben alves who was  a brazilian  educator so i listened a bit of him  and and this i didn't like so much it  was an audio book that i ordered from  brazil but i listened to a bit of it  but the point is oh and my reading  i don't have it all here i found some of  the portuguese books that i bought in  the past this is  unfortunately both these books are  translations these are books because  when i was in portugal i like to buy  books on subjects that interest me i'm  not normally a big reader of fiction  although i have a book by paulo cuello  and i must admit that i just don't like  his stuff very much  uh  so i read this book about the brain and  how the brain learns and stuff even  though it's a translation from english  so i read a bit of that to get myself  going and i also had because i'm  interested in russia and the soviet  union here's a book by martin amos on  stalin again in translation into  portuguese so it really doesn't matter  what you read  if you're exposing yourself to it all  the time i'm trying to notice  and and when i'm listening or when i'm  reading if i see  things that i know what that i have  trouble with like the subjunctive  subjunctive like verbs like which form  of the past tends to use when all these  kinds of things  that i will occasionally consult with my  uh  you know teach yourself or look up my  table on my ipad  then when i'm listening and reading  i want to be paying attention and what  happens is that as i've said before it's  it's like a jigsaw puzzle as more of the  pieces fall into place you're able to  notice more and more things  uh it's not because you saw an  explanation or saw a declension table  that you're going to remember it but as  you are now let's say very comfortable  with a certain case  or you know where not case but a certain  tense or certain vocabulary items then  other things that were just lost in all  the stuff you couldn't really understand  or  whatever make sense of  now those things start to stand out and  you start to notice them so th